### Experimental spell checking {#2.5.5-spell-checking}

<div class="changelog-entry">

Added experimental spell checker support. Unless you're on Linux, this
currently requires you to bring your own dictionary.

We intend to explore the possibility of including some common dictionaries
into Chatterino so you don't have to bring your own.

You can find all spell checker options under the <strong>External tools</strong> settings page.

{{ figure("/img/changelog/2.5.5/spellcheck.png") }}

{{ credit(author="Nerixyz, 4rneee", helper="pajlada, 2547techno", prs="6446, 6703, 6722, 6730, 6731, 6779, 6780, 6822, 6751") }}

</div>

### Polls, predictions, and suspicious users {#2.5.5-polls-predictions-sus-users}

<div class="changelog-entry">

Streamers can now use `/poll`, `/cancelpoll`, and `/endpoll` to manage polls inside Chatterino.

<br />

Examples:

- Start a poll for what game to play:  
  `/poll --title "what game to play today" --duration 60 --choice "expedition 33" --choice "eu5" --choice "disco elysium" --points 69`
- Cancel the poll you just started:  
  `/cancelpoll`
- End the poll, preventing further votes from coming in and showing some poll information in chat:  
  `/endpoll`

{% filter callout("note") %}
  If you would like this feature for moderators, please see
  <a href="https://twitch.uservoice.com/forums/310213-developers/suggestions/43347684-allow-channel-moderators-to-control-polls-predicti">this Twitch UserVoice</a>.
{% endfilter %}

{{ credit(author="iProdigy", helper="Nerixyz, pajlada", prs="6583, 6605") }}

</div>

<div class="changelog-entry">

Streamers can now use `/prediction`, `/cancelprediction`, `/lockprediction`, and `/completeprediction` to manage predictions inside Chatterino.

<br />

Examples:

- Start a prediction for what programming language to use:  
  `/prediction --title "what lang will i use today" --duration 5m --choice "golang" --choice "kotlin" --choice "rust"`
- Lock the prediction votes early:  
  `/lockprediction`
- Cancel the prediction, refunding all points:  
  `/cancelprediction`
- Complete the prediction, declaring a winner:  
  `/completeprediction --choice "rust"`

{% filter callout("note") %}
  If you would like this feature for moderators, please see
  <a href="https://twitch.uservoice.com/forums/310213-developers/suggestions/43347684-allow-channel-moderators-to-control-polls-predicti">this Twitch UserVoice</a>.
{% endfilter %}

{{ credit(author="iProdigy", helper="Nerixyz, pajlada", prs="6583, 6612, 6632, 6749") }}

</div>

<div class="changelog-entry">

Streamers and moderators can now use `/monitor`, `/unmonitor`, `/restrict`, and `/unrestrict` to control the suspicious chatter list from Chatterino.

<br />

Examples:

- Restrict forsen from chatting:  
  `/restrict forsen`

{{ credit(author="iProdigy", prs="6750, 6785") }}

</div>

