### Plugins {#2.5.5-plugins}

<div class="changelog-entry">

In this update, plugins can make use of several new APIs:

- **Access and modify messages in channels**: New methods like
  [`Channel:message_snapshot`](https://github.com/Chatterino/chatterino2/blob/v2.5.5/docs/wip-plugins.md#channelmessage_snapshotn_items) allow plugins to retrieve all messages available in a channel. The returned
  [`c2.Message`](https://github.com/Chatterino/chatterino2/blob/v2.5.5/docs/wip-plugins.md#message)s can be queried (e.g. accessing individual elements). Except for their flags,
  messages in a channel can't be modified. However, you can replace messages in channels ([`Channel:replace_message`](https://github.com/Chatterino/chatterino2/blob/v2.5.5/docs/wip-plugins.md#channelreplace_messagemessage-replacement-hint)).

  {{ credit(author="Nerixyz", helper="Mm2PL, pajlada", prs="6353, 6650", inline=true) }}

- **Add links to message elements**: Many message elements in Chatterino can now have a link attached to them.
  These links can open a usercard, jump to a message, copy text, and more.

  {{ credit(author="Mm2PL", helper="Nerixyz, pajlada", prs="6386, 6527", inline=true) }}

- **Parse and serialize JSON**: Many APIs communicate through JSON. To avoid having to include a third party library
  every time, Chatterino now provides a built-in
  [`chatterino.json`](https://github.com/Chatterino/chatterino2/blob/v2.5.5/docs/wip-plugins.md#json-api) module that you can `require()`.

  {{ credit(author="Nerixyz", helper="Mm2PL, pajlada", prs="6420, 6530", inline=true) }}

- **Get the current Twitch account**:
  [`c2.current_account()`](https://github.com/Chatterino/chatterino2/blob/v2.5.5/docs/wip-plugins.md#current_account) gives you the currently logged in account and its ID.

  {{ credit(author="Nerixyz", helper="Mm2PL, pajlada", prs="6554, 6675", inline=true) }}

- **Traceback for protected calls**: When a function fails in protected mode with [`pcall`](https://www.lua.org/manual/5.4/manual.html#pdf-pcall),
  you often want to get a stack trace of where the error happened.
  To help with this, we now include [`debug.traceback`](https://www.lua.org/manual/5.4/manual.html#pdf-debug.traceback).
  You can pass this as the second argument to [`xpcall`](https://www.lua.org/manual/5.4/manual.html#pdf-xpcall).

  {{ credit(author="Nerixyz", helper="Mm2PL, pajlada", prs="6652", inline=true) }}

- **Display name change events**: Plugins can now get notified when the display name of a channel changes with
  [`Channel:on_display_name_changed`](https://github.com/Chatterino/chatterino2/blob/v2.5.5/docs/wip-plugins.md#channelon_display_name_changedcb).

  {{ credit(author="Nerixyz", helper="Mm2PL, pajlada", prs="6594", inline=true) }}

</div>

<div class="changelog-entry">

Some fixes to plugins:

- Fixed Lua errors from handlers of HTTP requests not being logged. {{ credit(author="Nerixyz", prs="6452", inline=true) }}

 </div>

The LuaLS meta files moved from `docs/plugin-meta.lua` to [`docs/lua-meta/globals.lua`](https://github.com/Chatterino/chatterino2/blob/v2.5.5/docs/lua-meta/globals.lua) because of the new JSON module, which has a separate meta file.

<br />

If you have ideas for plugins, check out [this
discussion](https://github.com/Chatterino/chatterino2/discussions/4999). For
an overview of proposed features, check out [the graph in this
comment](https://github.com/Chatterino/chatterino2/discussions/4999#discussioncomment-14093379).

<br />

You can find technical documentation for plugins
[here](https://github.com/Chatterino/chatterino2/blob/v2.5.5/docs/wip-plugins.md).

