### Packaging {#2.5.5-packaging}

<div class="changelog-entry">

- The oldest supported Qt version is now `6.7.1`. This likely only impacts macOS older than 10.15 which is no longer supported. {{ credit(author="pajlada", prs="6628", inline=true) }}
- We no longer support Ubuntu 20.04. {{ credit(author="pajlada", prs="6630", inline=true) }}
- We no longer support AppImage builds. {{ credit(author="pajlada", prs="6504", inline=true) }}
- Added a CMake option `CHATTERINO_EXTRA_BUILD_STRING` which allows the packager to provide an optional freestanding Qt-HTML string that shows up in the About page under the Chatterino version. {{ credit(author="pajlada", prs="6766", inline=true) }}
- Chatterino now requires C++23. {{ credit(author="pajlada", prs="6693", inline=true) }}
- Nightly builds no longer use the `modes` file to know they are nightly, a new build option is used: `CHATTERINO_NIGHTLY_BUILD`. {{ credit(author="pajlada", prs="6798", inline=true) }}

</div>

